{"step_index":288,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-07T21:01:48Z","content":"### 1. Frontend Inspection & Required Changes Summary\n\nBefore implementing the API connection, we inspected the React codebase under `scratch/nexus/src/` to map existing mock data usages and determine the minimal set of changes:\n\n| File | Purpose | Changes Made |\n|:---|:---|:---|\n| **`src/lib/api.ts`** *(NEW)* | Central API configuration and HTTP client | Configured base URL `http://localhost:8000`, typed API client functions for all 5 required endpoints, and custom `ApiError` handling. |\n| **`src/components/common/ApiStatusBanner.tsx`** *(NEW)* | Visual status banner for live API sync | Shows loading indicator (`Loader2`), connection confirmation, and a clear error banner with a \"Retry\" button when the backend is unreachable. |\n| **`src/pages/CasesPage.tsx`** | Investigation dossiers & case creation | Connected `GET /api/cases` on mount, wired `POST /api/cases` in the creation modal, and added loading/error states. |\n| **`src/pages/DashboardPage.tsx`** | Command dashboard & core metrics | Connected `GET /api/insights/case-sih-01` (metrics, crime patterns, threat alerts) and `GET /api/network/case-sih-01`, with graceful fallback. |\n| **`src/pages/NetworkAnalysisPage.tsx`** | Network topology graph | Connected `GET /api/network/case-sih-01` (serving NetworkX computed metrics: degree, betweenness centrality, clustering). |\n| **`src/pages/EntityProfilePage.tsx`** | Subject dossier and indicators | Connected `GET /api/entities/{id}` with dynamic refetching on subject switch, loading spinner, and error banner. |\n\n> **No UI components were removed and the visual design was preserved.**\n\n---\n\n### 2. Implementation Details\n\n#### Central API Configuration (`nexus/src/lib/api.ts`)\n```typescript\nexport const API_BASE_URL = import.meta.env.VITE_API_BASE_URL || 'http://localhost:8000'\n\nexport const api = {\n  // Cases\n  getCases: async (params?) => request<Case[]>(`/api/cases${params ? ... : ''}`),\n  getCaseById: async (caseId: string) => request<Case>(`/api/cases/${caseId}`),\n  createCase: async (caseData) => request<Case>('/api/cases', { method: 'POST', body: JSON.stringify(caseData) }),\n\n  // Network Graph (NetworkX)\n  getNetwork: async (caseId: string) => request<NetworkGraphData>(`/api/network/${caseId}`),\n\n  // Entities\n  getEntity: async (entityId: string) => request<Entity>(`/api/entities/${entityId}`),\n  getEntities: async (city?: string) => request<Entity[]>(`/api/entities${city ? ... : ''}`),\n\n  // Insights\n  getInsights: async (caseId: string) => request<CaseInsightsResponse>(`/api/insights/${caseId}`),\n  \n  // Health\n  getHealth: async () => request<HealthResponse>('/health'),\n}\n```\n\n#### Loading & Error Handling Pattern\nEach page follows a unified state lifecycle:\n1. **Loading State**: Displays a subtle syncing badge while fetching from `http://localhost:8000`.\n2. **Success State**: Displays a clean status badge (`LIVE BACKEND SYNCED // http://localhost:8000`) and populates live data.\n3. **Error State**: If the backend is unavailable or an error occurs, an error banner displays:\n   > `BACKEND DISCONNECTED: <error message> (Displaying synthetic baseline fallback) [Retry Button]`\n   It falls back to baseline synthetic data so the application remains functional.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Verification & Live Test Results\n\n#### 1. TypeScript Build Verification\nWe ran `npm run build` to verify there are no TypeScript or compilation errors:\n```\n> nexus@0.0.0 build\n> tsc -b && vite build\n\nvite v8.2.2 building client environment for production...\n✓ 1879 modules transformed.\ndist/index.html                   1.28 kB │ gzip:   0.68 kB\ndist/assets/index-B0MDST_N.css   38.12 kB │ gzip:   7.42 kB\ndist/assets/index-BHmhkDsn.js   387.27 kB │ gzip: 114.54 kB\n✓ built in 755ms\n```\n\n#### 2. Live API & CORS Connectivity Verification\nWe verified all 5 endpoints directly against the running backend with the frontend origin `http://localhost:5173`:\n```\nGET /api/cases             -> HTTP 200 OK, CORS: http://localhost:5173 (775 bytes)\nGET /api/cases/case-sih-01 -> HTTP 200 OK, CORS: http://localhost:5173 (773 bytes)\nGET /api/network/case-sih-01 -> HTTP 200 OK, CORS: http://localhost:5173 (4,603 bytes)\nGET /api/entities/ent-1    -> HTTP 200 OK, CORS: http://localhost:5173 (873 bytes)\nGET /api/insights/case-sih-01 -> HTTP 200 OK, CORS: http://localhost:5173 (3,535 bytes)\n```\n\n#### 3. Active Ports\n- **Frontend**: [http://localhost:5173](http://localhost:5173) (Listening)\n- **Backend**: [http://localhost:8000](http://localhost:8000) (Listening)\n\nYou can now open [http://localhost:5173](http://localhost:5173) in your browser to view the frontend live-synced with the backend.","thinking":"**Confirming Task Completion Status**\n\nVerification confirms the successful completion of all prompt requirements. Frontend design, UI components, data replacement, and API configuration are all finalized. The core objective of integrating the API has been met without violating the given constraints.\n\n\n"}
