{"step_index":311,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-08T12:57:16Z","content":"Both the **Frontend** and **Backend** are now hosted and running.\n\n---\n\n### 1. Active Live Services\n\n| Service | Local URL | Network / LAN URL | Status |\n|:---|:---|:---|:---|\n| **React Frontend** | [http://localhost:5173](http://localhost:5173) | `http://10.11.1.108:5173` | **ONLINE (HTTP 200)** |\n| **FastAPI Backend** | [http://localhost:8000](http://localhost:8000) | `http://10.11.1.108:8000` | **ONLINE (HTTP 200)** |\n| **Interactive API Docs** | [http://localhost:8000/docs](http://localhost:8000/docs) | `http://10.11.1.108:8000/docs` | **ONLINE (HTTP 200)** |\n| **Health Endpoint** | [http://localhost:8000/health](http://localhost:8000/health) | `http://10.11.1.108:8000/health` | **ONLINE (HTTP 200)** |\n\nBoth services are bound to `0.0.0.0`, which means you can access the frontend from any phone, tablet, or laptop on the same local Wi-Fi network using the Network URL.\n\n---\n\n### 2. One-Click Launcher\n\nA startup script has been created at:\n```\nC:\\Users\\Nityam Jaiswal\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\start_nexus.bat\n```\nWhenever you reboot or need to start both services together, simply double-click **`start_nexus.bat`**. It will automatically:\n1. Launch the FastAPI backend on port 8000.\n2. Launch the Vite React frontend on port 5173.\n3. Open your browser directly to the dashboard.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Deploying to the Cloud (Production Hosting)\n\nIf you would like to host NEXUS publicly on the internet, here are the recommended options:\n\n#### Option A: Vercel (Frontend) + Render / Railway (Backend) — *Fastest Free Tier*\n1. **Backend (Render / Railway)**:\n   - Root directory: `backend`\n   - Build command: `pip install -r requirements.txt`\n   - Start command: `uvicorn app.main:app --host 0.0.0.0 --port $PORT`\n2. **Frontend (Vercel / Netlify)**:\n   - Root directory: `nexus`\n   - Build command: `npm run build`\n   - Output directory: `dist`\n   - Environment variable: `VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://<your-render-backend>.onrender.com`\n\n#### Option B: Docker Container (Google Cloud Run / AWS ECS / VPS)\nIf you want a single `Dockerfile` or `docker-compose.yml` to package and deploy both services as containerized microservices, let me know and I will generate the configuration files.","thinking":"**Listing available hosting options**\n\nConsidering the user's hosting needs, the current setup includes local and LAN hosting, with specified backend and frontend ports. A one-click local launcher is available, and there are potentially cloud deployment options.\n\n\n"}
